; FBX 7.7.0 project file
; ----------------------------------------------------
; SYNTHETIC (batch R). Not produced by any DCC tool.
;
; WHY: `data/*.fbx` (690 files) contains no mesh with more than one skin deformer, and no mesh
; with zero vertices that still carries a deformer. Both are load-bearing in
; `ufbxi_evaluate_skinning()` (ufbx.c:25063-...):
;   * ufbx.c:25079 `if (mesh->num_vertices == 0) continue;`   -- needs a 0-vertex mesh that got
;     past the deformer test on the line above.
;   * ufbx.c:25126-25127 `// TODO: What should we do about multiple skins??`
;     `ufbx_skin_deformer *skin = mesh->skin_deformers.data[0];` -- only discriminable if some
;     mesh has >= 2 skin deformers.
;
; This file carries both shapes:
;   Geometry::TwoSkins  -- 4 vertices, TWO Deformer::Skin objects (SkinA / SkinB)
;   Geometry::EmptySkin -- 0 vertices, ONE Deformer::Skin

FBXHeaderExtension:  {
	FBXHeaderVersion: 1004
	FBXVersion: 7700
	Creator: "ufbx-cs batch R synthetic"
}
